#. Tag: title
#: translator-guide.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Translator's Guide to &kturtle;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you probably already know, the unique feature of the &logo; programming "
"language is that the &logo; commands are often translated to language of the "
"programmer. This takes away a barrier for some learners to understand the "
"basics of programming. When translating &kturtle; to a new language some "
"more files have to be translated in addition to the usual strings and "
"documentation. Yet most it is autogenerated by Rafael Beccar's scripts. "
"These scripts can be found in <userinput>kdeedu/kturtle/scripts</userinput>, "
"the files that needs translation can be found in <userinput>kdeedu/kturtle/"
"data</userinput>, in those directories you also find README files which "
"contains instructions for using/translating them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: translator-guide.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating a Directory to hold the Translated Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, you need to create a directory to store the translated files. Create "
"a directory called <filename class=\"directory\">kde-i18n/<replaceable>code</"
"replaceable>/data/kdeedu/kturtle/</filename> in your KDE SVN directory, "
"where <replaceable>code</replaceable> is your country code (the 2- or 4- "
"letter <acronym>ISO</acronym> code)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copy the <filename>Makefile.am</filename> file from <filename class="
"\"directory\">kdeedu/kturtle/data/</filename> into this directory. Open it "
"using your favorite text editor, replace all instances of <quote>en_US</"
"quote> in the file with your country code (the one used above), and save the "
"file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: translator-guide.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "How To Translate the &logo; Keywords (commands)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copy the <filename>logokeywords.en_US.xml</filename> file from <filename "
"class=\"directory\">kdeedu/kturtle/data/</filename> to the directory you "
"have just created, and rename it to <filename>logokeywords."
"<replaceable>code</replaceable>.xml</filename> where <replaceable>code</"
"replaceable> is your country code (the 2- or 4- letter <acronym>ISO</"
"acronym> code)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Translate the contents of the <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">keyword</sgmltag> "
"tag (&ie; the information between <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">keyword</"
"sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">keyword</sgmltag>) into your own "
"language wherever possible. Also, translate the contents of the <sgmltag "
"class=\"starttag\">alias</sgmltag> tag, (&ie; the information between the "
"<sgmltag class=\"starttag\">alias</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag"
"\">alias</sgmltag>): these are used as shortcuts for the keyword."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, translate <quote>while</quote> in: <sgmltag class=\"starttag"
"\">keyword</sgmltag>while<sgmltag class=\"endtag\">keyword</sgmltag>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please do not translate anything else and do not translate the English words "
"in <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">command name=\"english_word\"</sgmltag>: "
"these must stay in English."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Last bit: do not change the order of this file, this is needed for Rafael "
"Beccar's automatic translation generation scripts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:47 translator-guide.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Save your file as <acronym>UTF-8</acronym> (in &kate;, use <guimenuitem>Save "
"As...</guimenuitem> and change to <guilabel>utf8</guilabel> in the box on "
"the right of the file name)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:50 translator-guide.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Commit your file (add your filename in the <filename>Makefile.am</filename>) "
"or send it to Anne-Marie."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:53 translator-guide.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case of any doubt, please contact Anne-Marie Mahfouf <email>annemarie."
"mahfouf@free.fr</email> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: translator-guide.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "How To Translate the Syntax Highlighting Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Translating the <filename>logohighlightstyle.en_US.xml</filename> is a "
"breeze when using Rafael Beccar's script in <filename class=\"directory"
"\">kdeedu/kturtle/data/</filename>. Please make sure to read the README file "
"in that directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For backward compatibility with all people who do not want to the perl "
"scripted blessing mentioned in the previous paragraph, here the old "
"fashioned way of doing it:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copy the <filename>logohighlightstyle.en_US.xml</filename> file from "
"<filename class=\"directory\">kdeedu/kturtle/data/</filename> to the "
"directory you created to store the translated keywords file, and rename it "
"to <filename>logohighlightstyle.<replaceable>code</replaceable>.xml</"
"filename> where <replaceable>code</replaceable> is your country code (the 2- "
"or 4- letter <acronym>ISO</acronym> code)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In line 4 of the file, there is <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">language name="
"\"en_US\"</sgmltag>...: here you change <quote>en_US</quote> to your "
"language's <acronym>ISO</acronym> code (2 or 4 letters)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Translate into your own language the content of the <sgmltag class=\"starttag"
"\">item</sgmltag> tag (&ie; the information between <sgmltag class=\"starttag"
"\">item</sgmltag> and <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">item</sgmltag>). This "
"content must match the <filename>logokeyword</filename> file. For example, "
"translate <quote>while</quote> in: <sgmltag class=\"starttag\">item</"
"sgmltag> while <sgmltag class=\"endtag\">item</sgmltag> and leave the spaces "
"as they are (one at the beginning and one at the end). Please do not "
"translate anything else."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: translator-guide.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "How To Translate the Examples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Again this task is simplified a lot by Rafael Beccar's script in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">kdeedu/kturtle/data/</filename>. Please make sure to "
"read the README file in that directory, since some work still has to be done "
"after the example logo files are autotranslated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you followed the instructions, given in the README file that you found "
"in the scripts directory, you should now be almost ready. Please do not "
"forget to test the translated example logo code you created, since it is "
"very common that an error sneaks in. Also make sure the <userinput>Makefile."
"am</userinput> in <filename class=\"directory\">kde-i18n/<replaceable>code</"
"replaceable>/data/kdeedu/kturtle/</filename> is updated according to the new "
"files. For the Dutch the <userinput>Makefile.am</userinput> should look like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: translator-guide.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"txt_DATA = advertentie.logo driehoeken.logo krullen.logo tafels.logo \\\n"
"bloem.logo driehoek.logo logohighlightstyle.nl.xml pijl.logo vierkanten.logo "
"\\\n"
"kleuren.logo logokeywords.nl.xml randomnaam.logo vierkant.logo\n"
"txtdir = $(kde_datadir)/kturtle/examples/nl\n"
"\n"
"xml_DATA = logohighlightstyle.nl.xml\n"
"xmldir = $(kde_datadir)/katepart/syntax\n"
"\n"
"keywords_DATA = logokeywords.nl.xml\n"
"keywordsdir = $(kde_datadir)/kturtle/data\n"
"EXTRA_DIST = $(txt_DATA) $(xml_DATA) $(keywords_DATA)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here a description of how to do the translation WITHOUT the use of Rafael's "
"perl scripts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copy the English example files from <filename class=\"directory\">kdeedu/"
"kturtle/data/</filename> to the directory used to store the translated "
"keyword and hilighting files. Translate the filenames of the examples in "
"your directory: this will allow users to easily and quickly understand what "
"the example is about."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Translate the keywords in the examples, using those in the "
"<filename>logokeywords.xml</filename> for your language. The keywords file "
"file must be done, first, before translating the examples."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Save your file as <acronym>UTF-8</acronym> (in &kate;, use <guimenuitem>Save "
"As...</guimenuitem> and change to <guilabel>utf8</guilabel> in the box on "
"the right of the file name)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Commit your folder (add a <filename>Makefile.am</filename> inside) or send "
"it to Anne-Marie."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case of any doubt, please contact Anne-Marie Mahfouf, <email>annemarie."
"mahfouf@free.fr</email> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: translator-guide.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finally, if you want, you can add your own examples in this folder."
msgstr ""
